WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Zero kara kakedashite

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Start running from the beginning,

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
Omoi dake wo dakishimete

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
with nothing but your emotions in your hands.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Sonomama kakenukete

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Just keep running...

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
Itsumo koko de mitsumeteru

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
I'm always watching you from here.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
Hajimete deatta hi no manazashi wasurenai

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
I still remember your expression the day we first met.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
Taiyou mitai ni kokoro wo terashitekureta

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
It lit up my heart like the sun.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
Asu no yukue sagashite nayandeiru nara

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
If you're anxious about where to go tomorrow,

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
I want to become a beacon to you.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
Ima kimi no tame ni akari ni naritai yo

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Start flying from the beginning.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Zero kara tobidatte

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Let go of your current self...

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Ima no kimi wo toki hanachi

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
and fly towards infinity.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
Mugen ni habataite

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
I will always watch over you...

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
Donna toki mo mimaru yo

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
no matter how far you fly.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
Kitto zutto tooku made

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:41.290
The fundraiser performed by the Tsukikage Acting Troupe and the Ikkakujuu Troupe,

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:42.970
<i>A Midsummer Night's Dream</i>,

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:48.450
became a hit by word-of-mouth and their outdoor stage soon was packed.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:55.060
They won their bet with the Athena Theater's director.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:04.700
But afterwards, Maya was cut from the show.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:09.340
Why am I the only one getting cut?

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:15.740
What are you plotting this time, Mr. Heartless, Masumi Hayami?

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:20.320
I'll show you!

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:24.990
I don't care how many obstacles you place in my way; I'll keep heading towards <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>!

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:31.040
Episode 34 - Maya's Challenge

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.330
You've got it all planned out, haven't you, Mr. Masumi?

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:37.380
Excuse me?

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.680
You cut Maya from the Athena Theater production because you heard that...

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:46.100
the girl starring opposite Ayumi in <i>The Two Princesses</i> at the Nittei Theater dropped out.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:52.940
She'll try her hardest in the audition, just to prove you wrong.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:57.990
And then, she'll regain her competitiveness against Ayumi Himekawa.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:01.850
You have such a rich imagination, Miss Mizuki.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.350
Maya Kitajima wants to audition?

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:09.840
Yes. And there's this other girl from the Jets Troupe, called Reimi Fujikawa.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.050
She's coming for me!

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:15.170
Finally!

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:18.850
For the first round of the auditions,

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:21.400
we would like the prospective candidates to memorize these lines in thirty minutes flat...

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.270
and then act them out.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:28.930
"Poison. Nobody knows that I have this poison."

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:33.260
"That person's life, their fate, their very existence..."

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:36.700
"Betrayal and pride... You've always done whatever you wanted."

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:41.880
"Go ahead and laugh... this is my trump card."

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.640
These lines are easy!

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.390
You just need to get across the character's murderous intent!

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:52.150
This isn't easy.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:58.210
What kind of person am I trying to kill?

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:01.370
Is it a lover? A friend?

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:03.980
These words tell me nothing.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:07.700
Depending on who it is, the emotions behind the lines change entirely.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.470
Is there anything I can do?

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:19.960
There's nothing for you to do but watch over her.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:23.610
Yes, sir. I'll watch over her for you.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:24.990
Thank you.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:32.010
What kind of person am I? What kind of person am I trying to kill?

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:35.010
What is our relationship?

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:38.390
I'm candidate #1, Midori Kusaka. Thank you for having me.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.390
"Poison."

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:45.560
"Nobody knows that I have this poison."

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:51.170
"With this, I can control anyone's fate as I please."

00:04:51.570 --> 00:05:00.940
"Now, I have that person's life, their fate, their very existence in my hands."

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:05.120
"I won't take it anymore."

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:10.600
"Betrayal and pride... You've always done whatever you wanted."

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:13.820
"You've ripped my heart to shreds!"

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.980
"This is my trump card!"

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:25.590
"I'll wear my poker face and I'll appear the same as always!"

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:31.570
If it were me, what kind of situation would lead me to poison someone?

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:35.820
Let's see, I'd lace the poison into food or drink.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:38.220
I'd have to be in a kitchen and I'd be using a...

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:49.090
"When it enters the body, it pumps around the body as soon as it's been digested."

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:53.240
"The victim dies four hours later with the symptoms of a heart attack."

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:59.430
"The poison can't be detected when it's in the body and all you need is a couple of drops."

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:03.270
"And you only need to ingest a couple of bites of the laced food.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:05.900
"And then, it's all over."

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:10.390
"I'll finally be free from these chains of sadness!"

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:12.390
I'm sorry!

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.280
You're the final candidate, so please hurry.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.140
Yes, sir!

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:19.240
Wow, she's so awkward.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:21.690
I don't expect much from this one.

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:23.470
I apologize for my lateness!

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:25.520
I'm candidate #7, Maya Kitajima!

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:33.410
I may only have a few lines, but acting is acting.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:37.840
My audience is a collection of judges.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.520
Yes,

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:43.290
we act for our audience.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.180
She turned on the tap.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:13.870
A kitchen?

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:16.180
She's miming being in a kitchen!

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:33.900
"Poison."

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:38.470
"Nobody knows that I have this poison."

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:42.970
"With this, I can control anyone's fate as I please."

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:52.220
"Now, I have that person's life, their fate, their very existence in my hands."

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:55.420
"I won't take it anymore."

00:07:55.800 --> 00:08:00.270
The person she wants to kill is in the next room!

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:07.040
"Go ahead and laugh... this is my trump card."

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:12.960
"I'll wear my poker face and I'll appear the same as always!"

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:20.170
"Just one drop... two drops...

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:25.040
and then, one or two bites...

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.600
and it's all over."

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:32.600
"I'll finally be free from these chains of sadness!"

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:49.560
I almost <i>heard</i> her putting the bottle down!

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:59.140
"My trump card."

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.220
Thank you very much!

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:10.350
Um, yeah, thanks.

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:15.120
<i>The Two Princesses</i>
Audition
Round One
"Poison"

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:19.250
With just these few lines, she was able to turn this scene, <i>Poison</i>, into a one-woman show.

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:24.140
Well, that's the caliber of acting I'd expect from someone Ayumi Himekawa considers to be her rival.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:29.600
For the second round, we would like you to use this song as part of your performance.

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.610
You may sing along or dance to it, if you like.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:34.740
You are free to do whatever you like.

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:04.410
How can I entertain them?

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:07.670
How can I engage the audience?

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:25.020
Excuse me. Do you have any shoe polish I can borrow?

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:58.770
Um... so what will you be doing for us today?

00:10:58.770 --> 00:11:00.430
I want to paint this wall.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.440
Excuse me? Paint the wall?

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.300
She's got a brush and some paint.

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:35.860
Incredible. Her movements correspond with the music.

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:43.680
There's something in her way.

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:48.560
It's a car!

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:50.850
Yeah. She's trying to paint around the car!

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:16.300
I would have never thought of doing it this way.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:18.800
Congratulations for making it through the first round.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.450
May we hear your impressions so far?

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:22.720
Well, I was confident that I'd make it through.

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:25.390
Congratulations on making it through the first round.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:31.880
There's one person I know who is hoping this audition will restore your status in the acting world.

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:34.370
Mr. Purple Roses!

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:38.000
Will you say a word for him?

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:39.470
Absolutely.

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:42.950
I will try my best to get through the second round too.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:47.950
I think I might have worried you.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:49.030
I'm sorry.

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:54.910
But I'm all right now. I won't give up.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:59.020
So, just one last thing.

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:01.410
Please keep watching me.

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:05.250
Please... keep watching me always.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:07.730
Maya...

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:16.640
And now, we'll begin the second cycle of auditions.

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:38.510
To act, an actor must obviously have skill.

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:43.170
It also requires a powerful imagination, creativity, and sensitivity.

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:45.290
The theme is to evoke emotion.

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:49.780
Laughter, sadness, rage - any emotion at all.

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:54.460
We would like you to express an emotion through your acting.

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:03.970
There is only one condition. The waiter will stay in the scene as he is.

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:07.680
Other than that, you are welcome to use your imaginations to act out any scene you like.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:11.310
In addition, this stage isn't mandatory.

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:14.170
If there is anyone who feels they're not up to it, they're allowed to forfeit.

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:17.270
No way... Forfeit?

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:18.420
But...

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:20.520
Great!

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:25.830
I was worried that the second round would be really hard!

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:29.880
But I reckon I could do this exercise all day long!

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:34.740
All day long? I don't want to lose to this girl!

00:14:35.050 --> 00:14:38.880
Anyone who thinks they can perform this exercise, please raise your hand.

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:40.170
Me!

00:14:56.850 --> 00:15:02.270
"I like how he orders me a three-course French meal as our breakup date!"

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:04.660
"He was the one who invited <i>me</i>, too."

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:08.290
"The meal's over and he's not even here yet!"

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:20.480
"I actually wanted to mend our relationship over our meal."

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:23.740
"I didn't want this to be our final date."

00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:28.130
"They're closing now."

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:37.360
"Farewell!"

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:44.920
That was some very natural acting.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:46.510
Yeah, she was good.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:48.930
Next up, we have Maya Kitajima.

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:49.920
Yes, sir!

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:55.150
"Ready or not!"

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:59.180
"Here I come!"

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:10.060
"He's here! Ha! He won't find me that easily!"

00:16:12.190 --> 00:16:14.530
"Oh no, it's the waiter!"

00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:19.540
"Weddings are so boring."

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:26.430
"Oh, it's the guy I ran into in the lobby."

00:16:26.430 --> 00:16:29.100
"Is he looking for me?"

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:33.830
"When I ran into him earlier, he dropped something..."

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:36.620
"A gun."

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:37.800
"A real gun."

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:49.370
"He's really looking for me!"

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:50.610
"What should I do?"

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:52.940
"He's coming this way!"

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:57.520
"He's looking under the tables!"

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:01.040
"He's going to find me..."

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:04.180
"He's going to <i>find me</i>!"

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:06.770
I'm on pins and needles.

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:08.710
The air's so tense.

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:11.060
"He's coming!"

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:18.830
"Music! The restaurant must be opening."

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:23.920
"The waiters and customers are coming in.... Thank God!"

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:25.940
"I have to go to the police."

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:28.400
"I have to make sure he doesn't find me."

00:17:29.890 --> 00:17:33.510
"But it's all right - I'm a pro at hide-and-seek!"

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:36.650
"Ready or not!"

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.750
"Here I come!"

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:50.070
Can we have the next person please?

00:17:50.390 --> 00:17:52.000
Come on, Midori!

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:54.390
But what am I supposed to do?

00:17:54.390 --> 00:17:56.070
Do whatever you want!

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:57.650
It's better than forfeiting!

00:17:57.650 --> 00:17:59.720
Is there anyone else who thinks they can manage a scene?

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:00.650
Yes!

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:07.510
I can! I can!

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:12.450
Ms. Tsukikage.

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:16.230
How are the auditions going?

00:18:16.230 --> 00:18:21.810
Well, Maya Kitajima just asked to do the second round exercise again.

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:22.990
Again?

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:25.190
She wants to do it again?

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:47.990
What's this? How does she come up with this stuff?

00:18:57.630 --> 00:18:59.270
I didn't see that coming!

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:02.090
So, she's playing his shadow? Well acted out!

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:29.400
The shadow suddenly took the place of a person!

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:31.630
That was a good one.

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:35.730
To create emotion out of a perfectly ordinary scene.

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:37.890
It happens to be her specialty.

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:43.160
She can do this more than twice - more than ten or twenty times-

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:46.390
she could do this exercise all day and never repeat herself.

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:48.090
You don't say!

00:19:48.090 --> 00:19:49.630
So, who'd like to try now?

00:19:49.630 --> 00:19:50.470
I'll do it!

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:55.970
Are you sure you can come up with a different scene?

00:19:56.510 --> 00:19:57.540
Yes!

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:01.770
Is she really going to do this exercise more than three times?

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:03.480
Yup.

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:08.230
Maya could do this all day long.

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:19.100
That girl has a thousand different masks.

00:20:31.630 --> 00:20:36.560
I should know. I know how frightening this girl can be!

00:20:37.560 --> 00:20:41.210
First, she played a child playing hide-and-seek in a restaurant.

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:44.610
Then, she did an abstract performance of a shadow.

00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:49.060
Next, a last supper before an imminent death.

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:55.020
Then, she played a ambitious boy plotting to take the place of his boss.

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:59.920
Her last scene featured a robotic customer in a futuristic restaurant.

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:03.430
Her acting really is something.

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:07.930
It shows off her limitless imagination and talent.

00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:10.520
She won by a landslide.

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:13.500
I already knew that would happen.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:16.590
She's going to join rehearsals in two weeks' time, so good luck.

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:22.970
Maya Kitajima, you're finally here!

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:26.550
You're finally facing me!

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:29.470
I'm so happy...

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:32.480
that I get to act opposite Ayumi again!

00:21:33.010 --> 00:21:34.720
I'm the second princess!

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:40.970
Maya won the role opposite Ayumi with her overwhelming talent.

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:48.780
What trials lie in store now that she's working with the extremely competitive Ayumi?

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:18.080
Chikazukitai noni toozaketeshimau

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:18.080
I want to be close to you, but you're distancing yourself.

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:31.320
Dakishimetai toki wazato hanareteshimau

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:31.320
When I want to hold you, you deliberately run away.

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:44.070
Marude jishaku no N to N no you da ne

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:44.070
We're like two poles on a magnet...

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:55.190
Otagai amari nimo nisugita seikana?

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:55.190
Maybe we're too alike?

00:22:55.190 --> 00:23:09.920
Motto motto sunao na hitomi de mitsureba

00:22:55.190 --> 00:23:09.920
If you allow your eyes to see the truth,

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:21.510
Yodonderu izumi mo suki tooru hazusa

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:21.510
even quagmires will become crystal clear.

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:25.090
I've been waiting for you, Maya.

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:27.890
I knew you would come.

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:33.350
You're the only one even capable of competing with me on stage.

00:23:34.530 --> 00:23:38.230
You are the beautiful and radiant Princess Aldis,

00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:43.500
and I am the tragic Princess Orgeld who spent her childhood in prison.

00:23:44.260 --> 00:23:45.800
I'm going to perfect this role.

00:23:46.470 --> 00:23:48.850
Nobody will dare suggest I was miscast!

00:23:46.580 --> 00:23:51.580
Episode 35 - Aldis and Orgeld
